{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKSubstrateInstances","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKSubstrateInstances","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.cohortWitness_of_lt13","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.cohortWitness_of_lt13","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKSubstrateInstances.lean#L69-L76","doc":"A concrete `CohortRSKWitness` for every `n ≤ 12`: the cohort is the `partitionsOf n`\nenumeration with hook-length dimensions, its Burnside field the `decide`-verified\n`dim_validated_le12`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.instRSKBijection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.instRSKBijection","kind":"instance","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKSubstrateInstances.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rskBijection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rskBijection","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKSubstrateInstances.lean#L52-L65","doc":"**`RSKBijection n` for every `n`** — `dim := dimSYT` with the Burnside field supplied by\n`QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds`, the Robinson–Schensted proof.\n\nThis supersedes the four hand-registered instances that stood here (`n = 3` the deuteron `pn`\nchannel, `n = 5` the s5-so3 keystone, `n = 7` the defect-cubic sign flip, `n = 12` the top of the\n`decide`-verified coverage), each built from `rskBijection_of_lt13`. They are removed rather than\nkept alongside this one: the class carries **data** (`dim`), so two instances at the same `n` would\nbe an ambiguity even though both supply `dimSYT`.\n\n`rskBijection_of_lt13` itself is retained — at small `n` the enumeration route is cheaper and needs\nno RSK. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rskBijection_of_lt13","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rskBijection_of_lt13","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKSubstrateInstances.lean#L45-L50","doc":"**Genuine `RSKBijection` construction for `n ≤ 12`** — `dim` is the real SYT count\n(`dimSYT`, a `Nat.card`) and the Burnside field is the proved `rskBurnsideHolds_le12`, not the\naxiom.  The class previously had no non-vacuous instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_proved_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_proved_le12","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKSubstrateInstances.lean#L38-L43","doc":"**The substrate identity is a theorem for `n ≤ 12`** — the axiom-free counterpart of\n`RSK_substrate_axiom`, via the hook-length bridge + the `partitionsOf` enumeration bridge.\nCite this (not the axiom) for any `n ≤ 12` use.  (Stated with a bare `n ≤ 12` hypothesis for\nergonomics, per review; `rskBurnsideHolds_le12` is the `List.range`-shaped source.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}